# Cybernetics — File Management Module Design

> Status: **Approved design.** Implementation follows this document.
> Scope: a MinIO-backed object-storage infrastructure module and a user/agent-facing
> file-processor feature module.
> Stack additions: **MinIO** (object storage) · **`minio`** JS SDK · presigned-URL transfer.

## 1. Overview & Goals

Add production-grade file management to the existing NestJS 11 application in two layers that mirror
the established `infrastructure` vs `features` split:

1. **`src/infrastructure/file-manage`** — a low-level, MinIO-specific, `@Global()` module. It knows
   nothing about HTTP, database rows, ownership, or validation policy. Its only responsibility is
   *talking to object storage*, behind a narrow, swappable `ObjectStorage` interface. It ships an
   idempotent **init script** that provisions MinIO for this application (bucket, policy, lifecycle).

2. **`src/features/file-processor`** — the domain feature. It owns the `files` metadata table, the
   upload/download **lifecycle state machine**, validation policy, the **external REST API** (for
   users), and the **internal service** (for agents and data-pipeline modules). It depends on
   `file-manage`, `database`, and `queue`.

**Design principles** (inherited from the app design): one cohesive `@Module` per concern; strongly
typed config via `@nestjs/config` + Zod `registerAs`; DI tokens as string constants; provider
factories reading `ConfigService.getOrThrow<T>()`; `OnApplicationShutdown` for connection cleanup;
Drizzle code-first schema with `baseColumns` + `BaseRepository`; Terminus health indicators;
`docker-compose` for local infra.

**Key architectural decision — transfer is presigned-URL-only.** Object bytes never pass through the
Nest process for external clients. This is the most scalable choice (the app process is not a data
pipe) and it shapes the rest of the design: an upload becomes a three-step lifecycle, and validation
moves from Multer interceptors to *declared-metadata policy checks* + *post-upload verification*.

## 2. Tech Stack Additions

| Concern | Choice | Packages |
|---|---|---|
| Object storage | **MinIO** (S3-compatible), local via Docker | — |
| Storage client | **`minio`** JS SDK (ships its own types) | `minio` |
| Content sniffing | Magic-byte verification in the async job (defense-in-depth) | `file-type` |
| Transfer | **Presigned URLs only** (external); direct SDK streaming (in-process) | (via `minio`) |
| Metadata store | **PostgreSQL** via existing Drizzle wiring | (existing) |
| Async processing | Existing **BullMQ** queue (new `file-processing` queue) | (existing) |

`minio` is the only required new runtime dependency. `file-type` is used by the async processor for
declared-vs-actual MIME verification; it is optional and can be added when that check is enabled.

The `minio` client is wrapped behind the `ObjectStorage` interface so that swapping to AWS S3,
Cloudflare R2, or GCS later is a single provider change, not a rewrite.

